# Keep the image to what actually runs. `Dockerfile`'s `COPY . .` otherwise
# bakes in whatever happens to be sitting in the build directory — and since
# the build context is the PROJECT DIRECTORY ON THE PI, that meant the live
# database, every `workout.db.bak-*` snapshot, the Garmin credentials and the
# cached OAuth tokens were all being copied into an image layer. The runtime
# bind mount hid them, so nothing ever broke; they were just quietly there.
#
# db.js:8 mkdir -p's `data/` on boot, so excluding it here is safe whether or
# not the bind mount is present.

# Runtime data + secrets — provided by the bind mount, never by the image
data/
# The RepDB library is downloaded into data/repdb/ at runtime; a copy still
# sitting in public/repdb/ from the days it was vendored must not be baked in.
public/repdb/
.env
*.env

# OMV-generated compose files. Not read at runtime (docker reads them from
# the host), and they carry an "auto-generated, do not edit" banner.
compose.yml
compose.override.yml
workout-tracker.yml

# Built inside the image by `RUN npm install` — a host copy would clobber the
# native better-sqlite3 build with one compiled for a different arch.
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Docs and test harnesses. Nothing at runtime imports them; browser-test alone
# is ~9MB of node_modules plus an unbounded screenshot directory.
*.md
# `*.md` alone matches the ROOT only (Go filepath.Match, not gitignore rules),
# so a nested Markdown file would ship without this.
**/*.md
testing/
unused/
scripts/

# Not needed inside the image it builds
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
.git/
.gitignore
.claude/
